cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Cite this dataset if you evaluate log parsers on it.
title: SecOps-2k
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/TMFNK/LogParser-Dataset
url: https://github.com/TMFNK/LogParser-Dataset
authors:
  - name: TMFNK
    website: https://github.com/TMFNK
    affiliation: MbitAI
  - name: MbitAI
    website: https://www.mbitai.com
abstract: >
  SecOps-2k: 2,000 fully synthetic security/operations log lines
  (sshd, sudo, firewall, audit) with template annotations in LogHub
  format, shipped with tight and loose grouping variants, a seeded
  generator, and a Drain baseline scored with GA/PA/FGA/FTA.
keywords:
  - log-parsing
  - log-dataset
  - intrusion-detection
  - sshd
  - benchmark
  - synthetic-data
  - reproducibility
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A Large-scale Evaluation for Log Parsing Techniques: How Far are We?"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jiang
        given-names: Zhihan
    year: 2024
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.10828
  - type: article
    title: "LogHub: A Large Collection of System Log Datasets for AI-driven Log Analytics"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhu
        given-names: Jieming
    year: 2023
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.06448
